# 2026-04-06 16:21:34.048854
+OBJECTIVE
+
+Do a full compile-stabilization and repo-hardening pass for the entire HackerzArt project.
+
+The project root is:
+
+/Users/joshuadavis/startups/hackerzart
+
+Right now the recurring build failure is that many files exist but are empty or otherwise invalid, causing TypeScript/Next.js errors like:
+
+"File '.../page.tsx' is not a module."
+"File '.../route.ts' is not a module."
+"middleware.ts is missing expected function export name."
+
+Your job is to audit the ENTIRE repo and fix all of this in one pass so the app becomes a valid, buildable Next.js App Router project.
+
+CRITICAL CONTEXT
+
+We already attempted to create a premium startup called HackerzArt.
+Some files now contain working code.
+Many others are empty placeholders or invalid non-modules.
+Do NOT destroy the project direction.
+Do NOT wipe the repo.
+Do NOT replace everything blindly.
+Instead:
+
+1. inspect all files
+2. detect empty files, zero-byte files, placeholder files, invalid modules, and broken imports
+3. replace/fix them with compile-safe implementations
+4. preserve any non-empty usable work where possible
+5. make the whole app build
+
+PRIMARY GOAL
+
+Make the project compile successfully with:
+
+npm run build
+
+SECONDARY GOAL
+
+Keep the product aligned with the HackerzArt concept:
+- premium dark startup
+- ASCII / hacker / keygen / gothic / baroque / terminal aesthetic
+- Noaerth portfolio startup
+- App Router structure
+- dashboard + auth + marketing pages + API routes
+
+REPO-WIDE TASKS
+
+1. Audit the entire repo for all .ts, .tsx, .js, .mjs, and config files.
+2. Find every file that is:
+   - empty
+   - zero bytes
+   - missing exports
+   - syntactically invalid
+   - imported but not implemented
+   - causing “is not a module”
