+OBJECTIVE
+
+Redesign HackerzArt into a premium, visually distinctive, production-quality startup website.
+
+The site is live and working, but the current design is too plain and not yet aligned with the actual HackerzArt brand.
+
+We need to transform it into a high-end, colorful, premium cyber-art product website inspired by:
+
+1. 90s and 2000s hacker / keygen / warez intro aesthetics
+2. ASCII art and terminal signal systems
+3. the uploaded ornate monochrome black-and-white reference image
+4. the uploaded premium Noaerth website screenshots:
+   - strong large hero typography
+   - dark cinematic gradients
+   - polished card grids
+   - premium startup hierarchy
+   - colorful but controlled visual system
+   - modern venture-backed polish
+
+The result should feel like:
+“luxury cyberpunk creative tooling”
+“ASCII x premium startup”
+“Apple-level polish meets underground hacker art direction”
+
+CRITICAL DESIGN INTENT
+
+Do NOT make this look:
+- generic SaaS
+- cartoonish cyberpunk
+- amateur neon hacker UI
+- gamified dashboard junk
+- cheap glassmorphism
+- random gradients with no system
+
+Instead make it feel:
+- premium
+- dramatic
+- artistic
+- technical
+- mysterious
+- colorful but restrained
+- brand-defining
+- visually memorable
+- investor-ready
+
+VISUAL SYSTEM
+
+Use a premium dark base with elevated color accents inspired by the screenshots:
+- deep navy / black backgrounds
+- subtle indigo / cobalt / violet atmospheric gradients
+- controlled orange / coral / magenta highlights
+- occasional cyan / electric blue signal accents
+- elegant borders
+- premium shadows / glow
+- strong contrast
+- sophisticated layering
+
+Blend this with HackerzArt aesthetics:
+- terminal framing
+- ASCII previews
+- ornate linework inspiration
+- engraved/cyber-baroque mood
+- signal density
+- scanline/grid/code feeling
+- monochrome structure with selective color drama
+
+HOMEPAGE TRANSFORMATION
+
+Completely redesign app/page.tsx and supporting components into a premium marketing homepage with sections like:
+
+1. HEADER
+- polished nav
+- premium simple branding
+- clear CTA
+
+2. HERO
+- large high-impact headline
+- stronger brand story
+- beautiful color atmosphere
+- ASCII/terminal visual panel
+- richer call-to-actions
+- premium layout and spacing
+- this should become the signature visual of HackerzArt
+
+3. FEATURE / CAPABILITY SECTION
+- turn existing features into visually distinct premium cards
+- cards should feel like product modules
+- include stronger information hierarchy
+- add tasteful color variation across cards
+
+4. STYLE SYSTEM / AESTHETIC MODES
+- showcase Hacker / Keygen / Gothic / Baroque / Terminal as premium visual modes
+- this should feel like a product system, not a simple feature list
+- create visually rich cards with distinct moods
+
+5. GALLERY / OUTPUT PREVIEW
+- make this feel more like collectible digital artifacts / rendered signal pieces
+- premium grid inspired by the Noaerth portfolio cards
+- use tasteful visual variety
+
+6. HOW IT WORKS
+- premium step layout
+- clear but elegant
+
+7. COMPANY / PLATFORM VISION
+- explain that this starts as a generator and expands into aesthetic infrastructure
+- make it feel investor-legible
+
+8. FOOTER
+- refined, minimal, premium
+- subtle Noaerth company positioning
+
+COMPONENT WORK
+
+Repair or create premium versions of these if helpful:
+- Header
+- Footer
+- Hero
+- FeatureGrid
+- HowItWorks
+- AsciiPreview
+- GalleryGrid
+- PricingCards
+- InvestorNarrative
+- Button
+- Card
+
+If some of these files are currently missing or broken, create or replace them cleanly.
+
+ASCII / TERMINAL INTEGRATION
+
+The site should visibly feel like HackerzArt.
+Integrate ASCII/terminal motifs into the UI tastefully:
+- hero preview block
+- framed code/signal panels
+- subtle mono terminal text details
+- signal-style dividers or micro-labeling
+- avoid making the whole page unreadable
+
+TYPOGRAPHY + LAYOUT
+
+Improve:
+- hero scale
+- spacing rhythm
+- section padding
+- content width
+- card proportions
+- CTA hierarchy
+- overall balance
+
+Typography should feel:
+- bold
+- clean
+- premium
+- editorial
+- not noisy
+
+COLOR STRATEGY
+
+Use color with intention.
+Think:
+- monochrome structure
+- premium startup gradients
+- artistic card accents
+- portfolio-card-inspired color diversity
+
+Do not overdo it.
+
+TAILWIND / GLOBALS
+
+Update app/globals.css and tailwind config if needed to support:
+- premium background layers
+- reusable gradient utilities
+- glow treatments
+- grid textures
+- subtle noise/scanline effects
+- better typography defaults
+
+Keep everything build-safe.
+
+PAGE ALIGNMENT
+
+Also lightly upgrade these pages to match the new brand system:
+- /gallery
+- /pricing
+- /investors
+- /technology
+
+They do not need full redesign parity with the homepage, but they should visually align with the new premium aesthetic.
+
+NOAERTH POSITIONING
+
+Keep “A Noaerth company” subtle and elegant.
+Do not let it overpower HackerzArt.
